1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:01,867
Notary.

2
00:00:02,033 --> 00:00:04,833
No certificate, no money moves.

3
00:00:07,133 --> 00:00:09,833
AI agents are starting to move real money:

4
00:00:09,867 --> 00:00:11,967
refunds, plan changes, credits.

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,233
They learn how from API docs.

6
00:00:14,367 --> 00:00:17,533
But docs and real APIs disagree.

7
00:00:17,967 --> 00:00:20,900
We pointed our agent at two real APIs,

8
00:00:20,933 --> 00:00:23,367
Crustdata and Dodo Payments.

9
00:00:23,533 --> 00:00:25,800
Crustdata's own docs say a company lookup

10
00:00:25,833 --> 00:00:28,300
with no match returns an empty result.

11
00:00:28,533 --> 00:00:31,167
In our run, it returned an error instead,

12
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:33,867
and three documented claims didn't hold.

13
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:35,733
An agent that trusts the docs breaks

14
00:00:35,767 --> 00:00:38,200
on exactly these cases.

15
00:00:39,233 --> 00:00:41,933
Notary is an agent that won't touch money until

16
00:00:41,967 --> 00:00:44,367
it has proven how its tools behave.

17
00:00:44,467 --> 00:00:48,467
It reads the docs and turns every promise into a claim.

18
00:00:48,633 --> 00:00:51,500
Before each test call, it commits a prediction,

19
00:00:51,567 --> 00:00:54,533
hashed, so it can't change afterwards.

20
00:00:54,700 --> 00:00:57,433
Then it calls the API and compares.

21
00:00:57,600 --> 00:01:00,167
A Reflector proposes explanations.

22
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:02,633
A stronger Adversary, running on a different

23
00:01:02,667 --> 00:01:04,833
model, tries to refute them.

24
00:01:05,033 --> 00:01:08,033
In our runs, it narrowed all five beliefs

25
00:01:08,067 --> 00:01:10,000
instead of rubber-stamping them.

26
00:01:10,167 --> 00:01:12,400
What survives becomes a certificate,

27
00:01:12,433 --> 00:01:14,667
valid only where it was tested.

28
00:01:14,833 --> 00:01:16,367
And the rule is simple.

29
00:01:16,533 --> 00:01:19,367
No certificate, no money moves.

30
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:23,700
The Guard holds anything uncovered for a person to review.

31
00:01:24,767 --> 00:01:27,267
Dodo Payments is where the money moves:

32
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:29,733
refunds, credits and plan changes,

33
00:01:29,767 --> 00:01:31,567
run in test mode.

34
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:35,033
Notary certified four Dodo behaviors before

35
00:01:35,067 --> 00:01:37,733
trusting them, from page limits to wallet

36
00:01:37,767 --> 00:01:40,733
credit units and idempotency keys.

37
00:01:41,267 --> 00:01:43,900
Crustdata tells the agent who each customer

38
00:01:43,933 --> 00:01:46,633
is, so the right policy applies.

39
00:01:46,700 --> 00:01:49,633
The models run through a LiteLLM gateway,

40
00:01:49,667 --> 00:01:52,500
with Claude as the Reflector and Adversary.

41
00:01:52,633 --> 00:01:55,600
And Notary is built to run on AWS:

42
00:01:55,633 --> 00:01:59,733
deploy scripts for a read-only hosted API on ECS,

43
00:01:59,767 --> 00:02:02,900
and Amazon Bedrock as a drop-in model provider,

44
00:02:02,933 --> 00:02:05,967
so the agents and their models can run inside a team's

45
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,500
own AWS account.

46
00:02:09,533 --> 00:02:12,600
We used neatlogs to look inside every run.

47
00:02:12,700 --> 00:02:16,000
Each run is one trace: every probe,

48
00:02:16,033 --> 00:02:19,000
every model call, every guard decision,

49
00:02:19,033 --> 00:02:20,633
labelled by agent.

50
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:23,133
On the Crustdata run, the trace shows

51
00:02:23,167 --> 00:02:25,567
the probe for one disputed claim.

52
00:02:25,733 --> 00:02:27,233
Its prediction is logged,

53
00:02:27,267 --> 00:02:30,300
with its hash, before the call is made.

54
00:02:30,367 --> 00:02:32,900
The result came back inconclusive,

55
00:02:32,933 --> 00:02:35,567
so Notary resolved it the safe way:

56
00:02:35,667 --> 00:02:40,033
it abstained, and no payment can depend on that claim.

57
00:02:40,900 --> 00:02:44,133
Two more mismatches, lookups that error where the

58
00:02:44,167 --> 00:02:46,067
docs promise an empty result,

59
00:02:46,100 --> 00:02:47,467
are still open.

60
00:02:47,733 --> 00:02:49,567
Notary hasn't certified them,

61
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:52,633
so the Guard won't let money depend on them either.

62
00:02:53,167 --> 00:02:57,133
On the Dodo run, the trace shows the Adversary narrowing

63
00:02:57,167 --> 00:03:00,267
four beliefs instead of upholding them as written.

64
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:01,933
Wallet credits, for example,

65
00:03:01,967 --> 00:03:04,933
are in minor units only for US dollars.

66
00:03:05,100 --> 00:03:07,633
Notary resolved those by certifying only

67
00:03:07,667 --> 00:03:10,400
the narrower scope it had proven.

68
00:03:11,433 --> 00:03:14,133
Entire captured how Notary was built.

69
00:03:14,233 --> 00:03:16,600
Seven checkpoints tie each commit to the

70
00:03:16,633 --> 00:03:18,967
coding-agent session that wrote it.

71
00:03:19,133 --> 00:03:22,500
Notary also uses Entire's code graph to

72
00:03:22,533 --> 00:03:24,333
prove a safety property:

73
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:28,067
every call that can move money goes through a guard.

74
00:03:28,133 --> 00:03:30,800
Zero unguarded call sites.

75
00:03:31,833 --> 00:03:34,633
And Notary measures what certainty costs:

76
00:03:34,833 --> 00:03:39,633
about three cents of model spend and fifteen Crustdata credits per run.

77
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:42,500
It exports those numbers for cfo.ai

78
00:03:42,533 --> 00:03:45,433
to build the business plan on.

79
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:48,800
So here is what Notary proved.

80
00:03:48,867 --> 00:03:51,600
Three documented claims that didn't hold.

81
00:03:51,633 --> 00:03:55,567
Five certificates, each one narrowed by the Adversary.

82
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:59,667
Zero unguarded money calls, at about three cents a run.

83
00:03:59,833 --> 00:04:00,867
Notary.

84
00:04:01,033 --> 00:04:04,133
No certificate, no money moves.
